[
    {
        "content": "<p>I’m considering proving the three outstanding determinant statements for <code>E₆</code>, <code>E₇</code>, and <code>E₈</code> through a uniform family rather than by computation. Extending the existing diagram pattern to an <code>n × n</code> matrix for <code>n ≥ 4</code> gives the formula <code>det Eₙ = 9 - n</code>. The proof would use the leaf recurrence <code>dₙ₊₂ = 2dₙ₊₁ - dₙ</code>, obtained by Laplace expansion, with base cases <code>d₄ = 5</code> and <code>d₅ = 4</code>. Would a public definition of the generalized <code>E n</code> family be appropriate in <code>Matrix.Cartan</code>?</p>",
        "id": 612870305,
        "sender_full_name": "Eureka Zheng",
        "timestamp": 1785111919
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think this is a good idea. Some of the larger E series appear in infinite dimensional Lie algebras and hyperbolic reflection groups, and the smaller E series are used by people who blow up planes (meaning del Pezzo surfaces).</p>",
        "id": 612872524,
        "sender_full_name": "Scott Carnahan",
        "timestamp": 1785114524
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I agree with Scott that there is some nice general theory worth adding to Mathlib here but note that these <code>proof_wanted</code>s were closed by <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"584390\">@Paul Cadman</span> mere hours ago in <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/42119\">#42119</a></p>",
        "id": 612941525,
        "sender_full_name": "Oliver Nash",
        "timestamp": 1785147665
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Thanks both, and thanks for pointing out <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/42119\">#42119</a>. I have now rebased and kept the existing <code>norm_det</code> proofs of <code>E₆_det</code>, <code>E₇_det</code>, and <code>E₈_det</code> unchanged. The proposed contribution is only the general family <code>E (n : ℕ)</code> and the formula:</p>\n<p><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><semantics><mrow><mi>det</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi><mspace width=\"1em\"/><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\"> \\det(E_n)=9-n\\quad(n\\geq 3).</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mop\">det</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0576em;\">E</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0576em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">n</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">9</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">n</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:1em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">n</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">≥</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">3</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mord\">.</span></span></span></span></span></p>\n<p>Before I open a PR, does this API and its placement in <code>LinearAlgebra/Matrix/Cartan.lean</code> seem like the right direction?</p>",
        "id": 613018451,
        "sender_full_name": "Eureka Zheng",
        "timestamp": 1785169506
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>It will be clearer once you create the PR but for now that sounds like a good file to use.</p>",
        "id": 613024863,
        "sender_full_name": "Oliver Nash",
        "timestamp": 1785171597
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Thanks — I’ve opened draft PR <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/42157\">#42157</a>. It keeps the existing <code>E₆</code>, <code>E₇</code>, and <code>E₈</code> definitions and <code>norm_det</code> proofs unchanged, and adds only the generalized <code>E n</code> family and its determinant formula. Comments on the API and proof structure would be very welcome.</p>",
        "id": 613080282,
